WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.889
Good morning, Hank. It's Tuesday.
So earlier this year you and I had a photoshoot

00:00:02.889 --> 00:00:05.180
with the brilliant longtime nerdfighter
Ashe Walker.

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:10.460
And I was under the impression this photoshoot
existed to get like a semi-professional picture of us

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:15.680
that we could send out for formal media stuff
so we didn’t have to keep sending out this picture,

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:18.380
although it is by far
my favorite picture of us.

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:21.480
But then at the end Ashe was like,
“Now make a bunch of funny faces,”

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:27.800
and Hank, as you know I cannot make funny faces
or do anything else that even vaguely resembles acting.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:33.700
I am such a bad actor that my cameo in the film
adaptation of my book was cut from the movie,

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:37.680
although they did let me keep my wardrobe,
and you're darn right I'm wearing it.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:43.270
That’s right, Hank, I’m cosplaying Girl’s Father right now,
the role for which I was inexplicably denied an Oscar.

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:46.460
But anyway, Ashe told us to make
some funny faces, and I tried.

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:52.380
And then Ashe used those faces to make the
2020 Project for Awesome calendar, which is,

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:56.240
to borrow a phrase,
“a heartbreaking work of staggering genius.”

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:00.320
Each month, we are transmogrified in great
and terrible ways into various animals.

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:03.650
Lemurs? We got lemurs.
Elephants? Heck yes, we become elephants.

00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:10.430
Oh my God, this one is like the trailer for the movie Cats,
only self-aware and for the benefit of charity.

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:14.460
You can get the 2020 calendar right now at
projectforawesome.com/donate,

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:17.100
where there are also lots of
other amazing perks.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:21.280
My favorite is our spouses’ incredible spinoff
podcast Dear Katherine and Sarah,

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:26.160
but we also have a Project for Awesome poster,
a Project for Awesome t-shirt, a commemorative coin.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:31.120
You can also get a limited edition signed
vinyl of The Anthropocene Reviewed.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:34.500
And also, you know how the United States
continues to mint one-cent coins,

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:36.880
even though they cost
more than one cent to make

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:41.800
and do not facilitate the exchange of goods
and services, which is the point of currency?

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:46.410
Well, at the DFTBA warehouse in Missoula, Montana,
we’re crushing hundreds of these reprehensible coins

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:50.460
and turning them into beautiful souvenirs
for you and/or your friends.

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:54.200
And most importantly, lest the cost of producing
and shipping any physical perks you buy,

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:57.380
100% of the proceeds go to charity.

00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:59.720
During this first half of the Project for Awesome,
we are raising money

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:01.500
for Save the Children and Partners in Health.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:04.170
Awkward transition to the serious part of
the video.

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:08.260
I think it’s really important to understand where
that money is going and the good that it’s doing.

00:02:08.260 --> 00:02:13.660
I mean, in the last ten years, the Project for Awesome
has raised over 10 million dollars for charity,

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:16.590
and to cite just one example of
what’s happened in that decade,

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:21.640
Partners in Health has been able to help build
and support the Butaro Cancer Center in Rwanda.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:27.140
70% of cancer cases occur in poor countries,
and because access to care is so difficult,

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:28.760
outcomes are far worse.

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:34.090
For example, in the United States, many types
of childhood leukemia have cure rates over 80%,

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:38.440
while in poor communities, those same cancers
are virtual death sentences.

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:43.350
And the Butaro Cancer Center offers real hope, and it
hasn’t just treated thousands of people with cancer.

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:47.220
It has also helped to train many
healthcare workers in oncology.

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:51.080
Save the Children, meanwhile, has helped reduce
stunting due to malnutrition and helped to build

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:56.640
safe places for kids in refugee camps amid
the greatest refugee crisis since World War II.

00:02:56.650 --> 00:03:00.290
PIH recently released a video about
a Sierra Leonean woman named Mabel

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:02.780
who was diagnosed with HIV
while she was pregnant.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:06.000
“That day, I felt the world
is over for me.”

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.660
But Partners in Health helped her get access
to anti-retroviral therapy

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:15.060
and eventually to become a community health worker,
one of over 11,000 supported by PIH around the world.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:20.220
Now Mabel helps people with HIV and tuberculosis get
the care they need and reduce the risk of transmission.

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:24.260
And because she’s paid a salary, she’s
been able to send her kids to school,

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:28.860
and that is the kind of generational change
we’re trying to support with the Project for Awesome.

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:33.600
Also, right now every dollar you donate will be matched
by nerdfighters who’ve contributed to a matching fund

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:36.080
AND by donors to PIH and Save the Children,

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:40.400
so every dollar you donate
counts as $4 to those amazing charities.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:44.120
So yeah, go to projectforawesome.com/donate
now to donate.

00:03:44.129 --> 00:03:47.640
The P4A will officially begin on
Friday at noon Eastern Time.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:52.840
There will be a 48 hour livestream extravaganza
at projectforawesome.com/live.

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:54.600
Hank, I will see you then.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:58.460
P.S. Hank, we are going on tour in January.
Also, for charity.

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:00.080
Link in the doobly-doo for tickets. Bye!

